WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.720
 I think the biggest issue is that most people don't know what they use,

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:06.320
 because if you install a package, it can include additional packages.

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:11.200
 You install a package and then it's a dependency of someone else, so you can't even track it.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:15.520
 Even if you then just redeploy your project because you did a small update

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:20.240
 on something that doesn't impact anything, it reinstalls all the packages

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.640
 and it installs all the malicious code.

